{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['sources'] += [\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"vote_prevote_checks\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1663,\\\"end_line\\\":1710,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n]\nd['investigations']=d.get('investigations',[])+[{\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@resurrect\\\",\n \\\"id\\\":None,\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"When RestoreCommittedLogs makes a restarted leader forget a committed removal, does the resurrected voter let that leader commit and report success for entries that the configuration committed in the log requires another member (B) to accept?\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\",\\\"vote_prevote_checks\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\"],\n \\\"parent_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"Yes: A's in-memory configuration still contains the removed voter C, so A's commitment quorum is computed over {A,B,C} and an entry acknowledged by A and C counts as committed even though the configuration committed in the log is {A,B}; A applies it and the client is told it succeeded although B, a member required for any quorum of the committed configuration, never received the entry.\\\",\n \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Same cluster and stores with the flag on and off: shut down C, remove it, commit further entries, restart the leader, bring C back so it catches up, partition B, then apply one entry on the leader. Prediction with the flag: the Apply returns success, the leader's commit and applied indexes advance to the new entry, and the entry is absent from B (and from every quorum of {A,B}). Prediction without the flag: the leader's configuration is {A,B}, so the same partition makes the same Apply fail.\\\",\n \\\"disposition\\\":\\\"active\\\"\n}]\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@resurrect\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_resurrect_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\",\\\"vote_prevote_checks\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Three-voter in-process cluster {A,B,C} at protocol version 3 with 50ms timeouts. A snapshots, then C is shut down for its own removal, RemoveServer C commits with {A,B}, two further commands push the persisted commit index past the removal entry, and A is restarted on the same stores with RestoreCommittedLogs (case restore_on) or without it (control restore_off). The restarted A's configuration and peer count are observed against B's. Then C is brought back on its old stores so it catches up from A, B is partitioned from A, and one Apply is issued on A; the probe records whether the Apply succeeded, the entry index, A's commit and applied indexes, whether the entry reached B, and the FSM lengths on both sides.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"C is offline for its own removal, so it never learns it was removed; that is an ordinary operator sequence (a failed node is removed while down and then comes back).\\\",\\\"B and C both hold every entry up to the removal, so the entries, commit index and configurations come from real replication.\\\",\\\"After the partition, {A,B} is the configuration committed in the log (removal entry committed), so an entry present only on A cannot be committed.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No disk faults or message loss; the only partition is the explicit disconnection of B.\\\",\\\"The probe does not assert what happens after the partition heals, which is the subject of the dual-majority harness.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"peers\\\":3,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":50}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap of all three voters, real snapshot, real RemoveServer, real commits, real shutdown/restart of the leader and of the removed voter on the same InmemCommitTrackingStore/InmemStore/InmemSnapshotStore instances, real transport reconnection and real partition. No fabricated configuration or log state.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"before_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"before_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_write_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"before_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"b_has_c\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_write_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"before_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"b_has_c\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A restarted leader must not count a voter whose removal is committed in its own log.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the same restart without RestoreCommittedLogs keeps the committed membership.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_write_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_write_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"entry_on_quorum\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"An entry whose Apply reported success must be present on a quorum of the configuration committed in the log ({A,B} requires both members).\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_write_restore_off\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_write_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"write_applied\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with the committed membership the same partition must make the leader refuse the write.\\\"}\n ]\n}\ni=d['interpretations'][0]\ni['limitations'] += [\n \\\"The resurrected-voter decision consequence (a write accepted on the leader and the resurrected voter while the committed configuration requires B) is claimed from a construction-time run of the child investigation's harness plus source, with its retained receipt requested in this update.\\\"]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
